# Services registered with the legacy servicemanager.
#
# The legacy servicemanager (the one that runs on this device) resolves
# service names through plat_service_contexts + vendor_service_contexts.
# CAF only ships the mapping for the services below in
# device/qcom/sepolicy-legacy/common/vndservice_contexts, which is the
# file used by vndservicemanager.  Without the entry here the name falls
# through to the plat catch-all "default_android_service" and the
# registration is rejected with
#
#   avc: denied { add } for service=com.qualcomm.qti.qseeproxy
#      scontext=u:r:qseeproxy:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:default_android_service:s0
#      tclass=service_manager
#
# The type itself is declared by CAF in
# device/qcom/sepolicy-legacy/common/vndservice.te; service.te adds the
# service_manager_type attribute it needs to be usable here.
#
# vendor.qcom.PeripheralManager is not in this file: CAF maps it for the
# legacy servicemanager in
# device/qcom/sepolicy-legacy/legacy-common/service_contexts (as
# binder_per_mgr_service).  A second, different mapping of the same name
# stops the build with
#
#   Multiple different specifications for vendor.qcom.PeripheralManager
#     (u:object_r:per_mgr_service:s0 and u:object_r:binder_per_mgr_service:s0)
com.qualcomm.qti.qseeproxy                      u:object_r:qseeproxy_service:s0
